# cn() class order

When building `className` with `cn()`, split Tailwind classes into separate arguments grouped by category. Add a `// category` comment **inline at the end of each argument line**.

## Order

1. **layout** — flex/grid, alignment, gap, flex sizing, overflow, positioning (`relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`, `z-*`, transforms)
2. **size** — width, height, padding, margin (box dimensions only)
3. **typography** — font, text color, line height, truncation, text alignment (`text-left`, etc.)
4. **bg** — background fills
5. **shadow** — elevation tokens (`shadow-sem-*`)
6. **border** — borders, dividers
7. **corner radius** — `rounded-*`
8. **transition / animation** — `transition`, `duration-*`, `scale-*`, `opacity-*`, `animate-*`
9. **theme overrides** — dark-mode / `[html.figma-dark_&]:` variants
10. **interactive states** — `hover:`, `focus:`, `focus-visible:`, `disabled:`, `group-hover:`
11. **state variants** — conditional classes (`active &&`, ternaries)
12. **className** — caller override (always last)

Skip categories that have no classes. Do not combine unrelated categories in one string.

## Example

```tsx
className={cn(
  "flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0", // layout
  "px-2.5 py-1", // size
  "text-xs font-medium text-figma-text text-left", // typography
  "bg-figma-bg-secondary", // bg
  "shadow-sem-sm", // shadow
  "border border-figma-border", // border
  "rounded-md", // corner radius
  "transition-colors duration-150", // transition / animation
  "hover:bg-figma-bg-hover disabled:opacity-40", // interactive states
  active && "bg-accent-subtle text-accent", // state variants
  className,
)}
```

Convert template-string class builders (e.g. `buttonClass`) to `cn()` when touched.
